  {
    "episode_id": 72103,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72103.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "So can you help me out? Have you talked to anybody at the school? I know I talked to Robbie George yesterday, who was a guy who jumped on the bandwagon on Friday. He's very big in the Catholic Church. I think he's a chair of ethics. Can you help me out on that? At Princeton University? And I called him and he said, Glenn, How can I help? He said, I feel so horrible on Friday. I tweeted something that this has to stop. And he said, and then it wasn't until Sunday that I actually saw that there was extra video and I did my homework and he said, I feel horrible. I tweeted immediately a retraction. He said, but Nobody's willing to step up and protect these kids, and I said, it's worse than that. The parents haven't heard word one from the school in a, hey, we've got your back. The archdiocese is completely silent on this, and they're afraid of funding. They're afraid if they support the kids, the liberals will go away and stop the funding. If they don't support the kids, the conservatives will go away and they'll lose their funding. i mean",
