    "turn_text": "That was an important one. Thanks. Thomas Massey, really one of the good guys that we can trust in Congress, Thomas Massey, you can follow him at massy.house.gov or representative Thomas Massey. Thank you so much. Appreciate it. So imagine that your kid goes to Washington and you're proud of him because he's standing up for a right to life. And this happens. And now people are protesting your place of business because your son or daughter did this. Now, It's interesting to me that even with all of the information that is out there, that the press hasn't turned around. They've corrected and said, yeah, you know what? There may be more information out there. They haven't corrected it. These kids were heroic in the way they acted. In today's world, they were heroic. Nobody in the press is talking about Nathan Phillips. We are in about seven minutes. I'm going to give you everything you need to know about Nathan Phillips, which kind of changes things. Then I'm going to go take you at the top of the hour through the what's called the TikTok. So in about 37 minutes, we'll start going through minute by minute what happened with the video and audio evidence. Native American Nathan Phillips said, well, I heard somebody chanting, build the wall, build the wall. Well, guess what? We found it. We found exactly who was doing it. We have the video of it. Except it doesn't fit with the media narrative. You will not believe who did it. And yet these people, Nathan Phillips, the black Israelites, The Black Israelites are some of the worst, is one of the worst organizations of all time. Nothing is being said. Now imagine if that was a group of five Nazis who were saying the same thing, because that's about what Nazis would say, except it would instead of black, it would be white. But these were black nationalists. Imagine if those were Nazis. You wouldn't have even heard about the school. And yet, because of the press just saying, oh, you know what, there's really nothing here, these kids are still under threat to the place to where nobody, no staff, nobody is allowed on school grounds today. And let me ask you this, what does this do to any school that says, next year I'm gonna go March for life? Courage is in short supply. The courage of speaking up. The courage of standing up. The courage of being a man. You know what a man is? A man is a guy who stands up against all of the bullies and says, I will protect the weak. You gonna go for them? You gotta come through me. Anybody who, any man, who is not standing for the week of Covington school. You're not a man. You're still a boy. If you say, well, I don't want to get involved. I don't want to do this. You're a boy. This is man's work. This is women's work, not girls, not boys. This is women and men's work. You want to be an adult? This is what it means. This is when it counts. We are living in a society that is teaching everyone that is watching, that are not go protest, that are not, would you hand me that? Would you hand me that right there, Marissa? Thank you. The world is being taught right now, because this is the only reason why these kids were targeted is because they were wearing a Make America Great Again hat. Because you wear a hat that says who you are? That allows everyone to say, oh, you know what? You don't really count. You don't really get a fair hearing. I know who you are. Well, you know, it's that kind of attitude that makes Americans want to put on the hat. It makes Americans say, I need somebody like Donald Trump because the world is full of bullies and no one will stand up. Men stand up.",
